@startuml Ingestion Deployment Diagram
title Ingestion & Sync Stage - External Systems
skin rose
skinparam shadowing true

package "External Data Sources" {
  [Socrata SODA API\n(Seattle Open Data)] as soda_api
  [Local JSON File\n(export)] as local_json
}

package "External Services" {
  [Hugging Face Hub\nSentence Transformers] as hf_hub
}

package "External Database" {
  [PostgreSQL + pgvector\npermit_trade_skills DB] as postgres
}

package "User" {
  [Data Engineer] as user
}

' Data Sources
user --> soda_api : requests permit data\n(when API available)
user --> local_json : provides export file\n(--local-file)
soda_api --> user : returns permit rows
local_json --> user : provides permit data

' Embeddings
hf_hub --> user : downloads model\n(all-MiniLM-L6-v2, 384-dim)
user --> hf_hub : loads embedding model

' Database
postgres --> user : stores permits\n(sync upsert)
postgres --> user : stores sync_metadata\n(run reports)
postgres --> user : stores embeddings\n(description_embedding)
postgres --> user : status_history\n(status changes)

legend right
  <b>External Systems:</b>
  - <b>Socrata SODA API:</b> Live data source for Seattle permits (cos-data.seattle.gov)
    - Currently down - using local export fallback
    - Rate-limited with per-host limiter
  - <b>Local JSON:</b> Downloaded export for offline/sync testing
    - 193,249 rows for Seattle
    - Mode: full sync (no cursor)
  - <b>Hugging Face Hub:</b> Source for embedding models
    - Model: all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (384 dimensions)
    - Downloaded on first sync
    - HF_TOKEN env var for authenticated downloads
  - <b>PostgreSQL + pgvector:</b> Canonical data store
    - Tables: permits, sync_metadata, status_history
    - Vector index: none (exact scan for accuracy)

  <b>Data Flow:</b>
  1. Data Engineer provides data source (API or local file)
  2. System downloads embedding model from Hugging Face
  3. System reads permits and upserts to PostgreSQL
  4. Sync reports and status history stored in PostgreSQL

  <b>Configuration:</b>
  - Database URL: PERMIT_TRADE_SKILLS_DB_URL or --db-url
  - User-Agent: configured in ingest.user_agent setting
  - Rate limiting: settings ingest.rate_limit_per_minute
endlegend

@enduml